<div id="recipe-82806-ingredients" class="wprm-recipe-ingredients-container wprm-recipe-ingredients-no-images wprm-recipe-82806-ingredients-container wprm-block-text-normal wprm-ingredient-style-regular wprm-recipe-images-before" data-recipe="82806" data-servings="6"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-ingredients-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Ingredients</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-group"><ul class="wprm-recipe-ingredients"><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="0"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&frac14;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">cup</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">olive oil</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">plus more to oil the grill grates</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="1"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&#8531;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">cup</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">soy sauce</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="2"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&frac14;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">cup</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">apple cider vinegar</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">or balsamic vinegar or red wine vinegar</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="3"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">2</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">tablespoons</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">lemon juice</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">or lime juice</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="4"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">2</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">tablespoons</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">Worcestershire sauce</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="5"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">tablespoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">Dijon mustard</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="6"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">tablespoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">honey</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">or brown sugar</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="7"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">3</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">cloves</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">garlic</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded">minced</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="8"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">sweet paprika</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="9"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&frac12;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">ground cumin</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="10"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&frac12;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">kosher salt</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="11"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">&frac14;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">teaspoon</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">black pepper</span></li><li class="wprm-recipe-ingredient" style="list-style-type: disc;" data-uid="12"><span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount">1 &frac12;</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit">lbs</span> <span class="wprm-recipe-ingredient-name">flank steak</span></li></ul></div></div>
<div id="recipe-82806-instructions" class="wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-82806-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal" data-recipe="82806"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Instructions</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-82806-step-0-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Select a container that is large enough to fit your flank steak comfortably, ideally one with a fitting lid.  Alternatively, you can also use a resealable plastic bag.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82806-step-0-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Add in &frac14; cup of olive oil, &#8531; cup of soy sauce, &frac14; cup of apple cider vinegar, 2 tablespoons of lemon juice, 2 tablespoons of Worcestershire sauce, 1 tablespoon of Dijon mustard, 1 tablespoon of honey, 3 cloves of minced garlic, 1 teaspoon of sweet paprika, &frac12; teaspoon of ground cumin, &frac12; teaspoon of kosher salt, &frac14; teaspoon black pepper. Whisk to combine.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-flank-steak-recipe-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Flank steak marinade being poured over the meat." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-flank-steak-recipe-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-flank-steak-recipe-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-flank-steak-recipe-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-flank-steak-recipe-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-flank-steak-recipe.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-flank-steak-recipe.jpg"></div> </li><li id="wprm-recipe-82806-step-0-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Add the flank steak and ensure that the whole piece is submerged in the marinade.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82806-step-0-3" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Cover and refrigerate for at least 1 hour, preferably overnight, but no longer than 24 hours.</div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-media wprm-recipe-instruction-image"><img decoding="async" width="350" height="217" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-flank-steak-on-the-grill-350x217.jpg" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="Flank steak in the marinade and then on the grill." srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-flank-steak-on-the-grill-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-flank-steak-on-the-grill-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-flank-steak-on-the-grill-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-flank-steak-on-the-grill-150x93.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-flank-steak-on-the-grill.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Marinated-flank-steak-on-the-grill.jpg"></div> </li></ul></div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><h4 class="wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold">To Cook it on the Grill:</h4><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-82806-step-1-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">When ready to cook, preheat a gas grill to 500&deg;F.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82806-step-1-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Scrape the grill grates to remove any possible food residue. Dip a wad of paper towel into a bowl of oil and coat the grates generously with the oil.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82806-step-1-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Remove the flank steak from the marinade, letting the excess marinade drip off. Discard the marinade.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82806-step-1-3" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Place the meat on the grill and cook for 3-4 minutes on each side for rare (internal temperature is 130 to 135 &deg;F), 4-5 minutes on each side for medium (internal temperature is 136 to 145 &deg;F), or 5-6 minutes on each side for medium-well (internal temperature is 146 to 155 &deg;F).</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82806-step-1-4" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">When it reaches your desired doneness, transfer the grilled flank steak to a platter and cover it with foil.</div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82806-step-1-5" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;">Let it rest for 5 minutes, and then slice it against the grain. Serve while still warm.</div></li></ul></div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><h4 class="wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold">To Broil in The Oven</h4><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-82806-step-2-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Set your oven to the "broil" setting on high. For the best results, place the oven rack in the upper third section, about 5-6 inches from the heat source.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82806-step-2-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Line a baking sheet with parchment paper and set a wire rack over it.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82806-step-2-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Remove the steak from the marinade and let the excess drip off before transferring it to your prepared sheet pan. Broil for 5-6 minutes on each side, or until it reaches your desired doneness.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82806-step-2-3" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Transfer the steak to a plate, cover loosely with foil, and let it rest for 5-10 minutes before slicing.</span></div></li></ul></div><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-group"><h4 class="wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold">On The Stove Top</h4><ul class="wprm-recipe-instructions"><li id="wprm-recipe-82806-step-3-0" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Place a large cast-iron skillet over medium high heat and heat it until sizzling hot.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82806-step-3-1" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Remove the marinated flank steak from the marinade, making sure to remove any excess. Transfer it onto a clean plate and pat dry with a paper towel to remove as much of the liquid as possible.</span></div></li><li id="wprm-recipe-82806-step-3-2" class="wprm-recipe-instruction" style="list-style-type: decimal;"><div class="wprm-recipe-instruction-text" style="margin-bottom: 5px;"><span style="display: block;">Transfer the steak to the skillet and sear for 3-4 minutes or until nicely browned. Flip the steak and cook for another 3-5 minutes, depending on the level of doneness you prefer.</span></div></li></ul></div></div>
<div id="wprm-recipe-video-container-82806" class="wprm-recipe-video-container"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-video-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Video</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-video"><iframe loading="lazy" title="The Only Flank Steak Marinade You Need (Served Over a Summer Salad)" width="800" height="450" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/GtMWUdH1vOw?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe></div></div>
<div id="recipe-82806-notes" class="wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal"><h3 class="wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none" style="">Notes</h3><div class="wprm-recipe-notes"><ul>
<li><strong>Let it come to room temperature before grilling:</strong> If you are marinating your steak overnight, take it out of the fridge and let it rest on the counter 30 to 60 minutes before grilling. If you put cold marinated steak on a hot grill, it won&rsquo;t sear properly. It&rsquo;s likely that the outside will cook before the inside is cooked.</li>
<li><strong>Level of doneness:</strong> Please use the grilling times I listed in the post as a place to start. The grilling time could change based on the thickness of your flank steak. The best way to check doneness is with a meat thermometer.</li>
<li><strong>Storage:</strong> If you&rsquo;re planning to store leftovers, I recommend keeping the steak whole. Once it&rsquo;s cooled, wrap it up or transfer it to an airtight container and store it in the fridge for up to 3 days. If it&rsquo;s already sliced, that&rsquo;s okay too. Place it in an airtight container and store it in the fridge for up to 3 days.</li>
</ul></div></div>
